# The CLI uploads from the repo root (pnpm needs the workspace root to resolve
# `workspace:` deps), but the build's Root Directory is apps/web — so
# everything the web app doesn't need is dead weight. Without this the upload
# aborts: pipeline/ alone is ~9GB of captures, frames and checkpoints.

# GPU pipeline: Python worker, source videos, frames, checkpoints, PLYs.
# Never built or served by the web app.
pipeline

# The standalone viewer app and its own copies of the models. The web app
# serves its own from apps/web/public.
apps/viewer

# Source captures at the repo root: 777MB + 427MB + 322MB. These are the
# pipeline's *input*, nothing serves them, and each one is over Vercel's 100MB
# per-file limit — they were the whole of the 1.5GB the first upload pushed.
*.mp4

# Secrets. `vercel link` writes a VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN into .env.local, and env
# vars belong in project settings rather than the upload.
.env
.env.*

.pytest_cache

# Build output and dependencies — Vercel installs and builds these itself.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.claude
